// EU07 / 303E main traction circuit, for Knsgf's electric_sim circuit compiler
// (Derail_Valley_electric_concept, CC0 / MIT).
//
// GENERATED by build_circuit.py - change the wiring there, not here.
//
// Wiring: real, from sheet 4 of the 303E schemat ideowy (zm. 37); checked against the
// sheet 3 programme (1 ohm each: 30 -> 1 over 1-27, 0 at 28, 7.0 -> 0.5 over 29-42, 0 at 43).
//
//   LINE - SL1 - R25 - R5 - [motors 1,2] - M1 - R3 R7 R9 ... R29 - X
//   X - IR2 - earth (parallel)            X - IS - R1 - R2 - N4 (series)
//   LINE - SL3 - IR1 - N4 (parallel)      N4 - R4 R6 ... R26 - Z - [motors 3,4] - M2 - R28 - R30 - earth
//   M1 - IM - Z (the bridge, position 28)
//
// SRn bridges its Rn; SR29 and SR26 bridge a whole ladder.
// Motor pair: two armatures in series, fields inside the reverser (NW1-NW8, field side),
// six shunt steps SPn + RPn, inductive shunt I across reverser + fields.
// OS1/OS3 isolate a pair, OS2/OS4 bypass it.
//
// Layout: compiler cannot turn corners - every node a vertical bus, every element its own row.
//
// Numbers: starting resistors from design_resistors.py, scaled; field shunts from DTR
// percentages; supply and pantograph placeholders (docs/NOTES.md).
// Not modelled: SDS1/RDS1, SDS2/RDS2 (field mid-point shunts), armature voltage relays,
// ammeter shunts.

